 "notes_path": "history/polities/_notes/am-04.md",
 "problems": [
  "chimu-empire is NOT a separate dossier: Cliopatria rows Chimor (911-1187) and Chimu Empire (1188-1481) share Wikidata Q581741 and one article; one dossier chimor reviews all seven shapes of both rows (assignment table listed both slugs).",
  "Cliopatria's Chimu Empire 1475 shape is marked wrong (Inca hold the coast from 1470/71) and the Inca Empire 1534 shape keeps the whole empire to 1539 although the Spanish held Cajamarca, Cusco, Lima and Quito by 1535-37; the Spanish Empire dossier (am-06) needs mirror events.",
  "Three cosmetic validator warnings remain: cuzco war 1438, lupaca-kingdom war 1473 and chachapoya-culture war 1493-1527 fall outside the states' independent lives.",
  "WebFetch returns summaries: quotes in notes are the tool's returned sentences; where only a paraphrase came back (Chan Chan on the Inca conquest of Chimor, Spanish conquest page on Quito) the dossier says paraphrase.",
  "Page budget exceeded on inca-empire (sixteen pages against an allowance of five) because the orchestrator note put the civil war, Spanish conquest and Vilcabamba in this group; no keyframe is marked unverified: page budget.",
  "Atahualpa's execution is 26 July 1533 on his own page and 29 August on the Civil War and Spanish conquest pages; the dossiers use July and the notes record August."
 ]
}